  "notes": "Benchmark (a), the 9 V 555 blinker. Transcribed from ir/examples/blinker.ir.json, which was authored under AMB-38 (IR v0) and committed before this issue existed. That is the whole point of the anchor: a bake-off whose reference netlist was written by the same hand as its parsers proves nothing, so this design's ground truth comes from somewhere the bake-off cannot reach. lang/tests/test_bakeoff.py elaborates this model, flattens it, and requires the result to reproduce that IR document's instances, nets, connections and assertions exactly.\n\nAC5a runs its trials on design (a), so this is the design the candidate grammars will actually be judged on by a model in AMB-33/R37. It is small, which is the point: if a grammar cannot express a 555 blinker cheaply and legibly, nothing else about it matters.\n\nWhat the IR document carries and this model deliberately does not: header hashes, generator identity, and the flattened net membership of module-internal ports. Those are elaboration outputs, not source-level facts, and putting them in a source model would be writing the answer down twice.",
